description:
Get a pilot run's live status board — its per-document status and run-level counts (#252).

Use after handinloop_submit_pilot_batch to watch the batch clear: documents move queued -> in_review -> completed | rejected. The run is done when counts.completed + counts.rejected == counts.total.

in_review covers two stages: the worker still extracting and checking a document, then a person reviewing it. counts.awaiting_human is how many of the in_review documents a person has; the rest (in_review - awaiting_human) are still with the worker.

Args:
  - pilot_run_id: the run to check (must belong to your account).

Returns: {
  pilot_run: { id, name, task_type, status },
  items: [{ job_id, file_name?, status, submitted_at, finished_at? }],
  counts: { total, queued, in_review, awaiting_human, completed, rejected }
}
